From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Schmiedel <Martin.Schmiedel@tq-group.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:49:10 +0200
Subject: net: imx9: dwc_eth_qos: support external RMII REF_CLK source

imx93_eqos_interface_init() always leaves the MAC's REF_CLK source mux
selecting the internally generated clock, matching NXP's reference
topology where the SOC is RMII clock master. Boards where the PHY
itself is REF_CLK master (its own crystal, feeding REF_CLK into the
SOC) need the adjacent enet_clk_sel register switched to the external
source instead, or the EQOS never comes up correctly.

Add the "snps,rmii_refclk_ext" devicetree property (same name and
semantics as Linux's dwmac-imx imx93_set_intf_mode()) to opt into this;
default behavior for all other boards is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Martin Schmiedel <Martin.Schmiedel@tq-group.com>
---
 arch/arm/include/asm/arch-imx9/imx-regs.h |  1 +
 arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/native/clock.c     | 12 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-imx9/imx-regs.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-imx9/imx-regs.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-imx9/imx-regs.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-imx9/imx-regs.h
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@
 #define BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_INTF_SEL_RMII         (0x4 << 1)
 #define BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_INTF_SEL_RGMII        (0x1 << 1)
 #define BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_CLK_GEN_EN            (0x1 << 0)
+#define BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_CLK_SEL_EXT           (0x1 << 0)
 
 #define MARKETING_GRADING_MASK	GENMASK(5, 4)
 #define SPEED_GRADING_MASK	GENMASK(11, 6)
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/native/clock.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/native/clock.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/native/clock.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/native/clock.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <asm/global_data.h>
 #include <asm/io.h>
 #include <div64.h>
+#include <dm/read.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
@@ -915,6 +916,17 @@ static int imx93_eqos_interface_init(struct udevice *dev, phy_interface_t interf
 			     BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_CLK_GEN_EN);
 		break;
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RMII:
+		/*
+		 * On boards where the PHY is REF_CLK master (its own crystal,
+		 * feeding REF_CLK into the SOC), the MAC's REF_CLK source mux
+		 * (the register right after eqos_gpr) must be switched to the
+		 * external pin - matches Linux's imx93_set_intf_mode()
+		 * (drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-imx.c). CLK_GEN_EN
+		 * is set unconditionally either way, same as Linux does.
+		 */
+		if (dev_read_bool(dev, "snps,rmii_refclk_ext"))
+			clrbits_le32(&bctrl->enet_clk_sel,
+				     BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_CLK_SEL_EXT);
 		setbits_le32(&bctrl->eqos_gpr,
 			     BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_INTF_SEL_RMII |
 			     BCTRL_GPR_ENET_QOS_CLK_GEN_EN);
